110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 75 0 R
/T (Moderncloud applications host highly dynamic web services that experience continuously changing and unpredictable user workloads. Traditional reactive auto-scaling models \(e.g., standard Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler\) trigger infrastructure adjustments only after physical metric thresholds \(such as CPU utilization exceeding 80%\) are breached. Because launching new container replicas or virtual machines incurs a non-negligible initialization lag \(ranging from 30 to 180 seconds\), reactive systems respond too late during high-velocity burst traffic. This provisioning delay results in transient resource exhaustion, latency spikes, and severe Service Level Agreement \(SLA\) violations. )
/E (Moderncloud applications host highly dynamic web services that experience continuously changing and unpredictable user workloads. Traditional reactive auto-scaling models \(e.g., standard Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler\) trigger infrastructure adjustments only after physical metric thresholds \(such as CPU utilization exceeding 80%\) are breached. Because launching new container replicas or virtual machines incurs a non-negligible initialization lag \(ranging from 30 to 180 seconds\), reactive systems respond too late during high-velocity burst traffic. This provisioning delay results in transient resource exhaustion, latency spikes, and severe Service Level Agreement \(SLA\) violations. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
