114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 75 0 R
/T (Historically,cloudoperators manage volatility using static provisioning or threshold-based reactive auto- scaling. Static provisioning maintains fixed peak capacity, incurring massive financial waste during off- peak periods. Reactive scaling triggers pod instantiation only after overload occurs, creating a 1 to 3 minute vulnerability window where end users suffer request timeouts and degraded performance. )
/E (Historically,cloudoperators manage volatility using static provisioning or threshold-based reactive auto- scaling. Static provisioning maintains fixed peak capacity, incurring massive financial waste during off- peak periods. Reactive scaling triggers pod instantiation only after overload occurs, creating a 1 to 3 minute vulnerability window where end users suffer request timeouts and degraded performance. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 75 0 R
/T (This research project aims to design, implement, and validate an intelligent, closed-loop demand prediction and proactive auto-scaling framework for dynamic cloud infrastructure. By replacing standard reactive mechanisms with predictive time-series deep learning architectures \(including Gated Recurrent Units [GRU] and Long Short-Term Memory [LSTM] networks\), the system anticipates workload spikes 3 to 5 minutes into the future. The scaling engine programmatically communicates with the Kubernetes API to adjust container pod replicas pre-emptively, eliminating cold-start delays, preventing SLA penalties, and optimizing overall operational costs and cluster energy consumption. )
/E (This research project aims to design, implement, and validate an intelligent, closed-loop demand prediction and proactive auto-scaling framework for dynamic cloud infrastructure. By replacing standard reactive mechanisms with predictive time-series deep learning architectures \(including Gated Recurrent Units [GRU] and Long Short-Term Memory [LSTM] networks\), the system anticipates workload spikes 3 to 5 minutes into the future. The scaling engine programmatically communicates with the Kubernetes API to adjust container pod replicas pre-emptively, eliminating cold-start delays, preventing SLA penalties, and optimizing overall operational costs and cluster energy consumption. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 75 0 R
/T (Infrastructural Volatility Management: Overcoming the physical spin-up and readiness probe delays inherent in microservices container orchestration. )
/E (Infrastructural Volatility Management: Overcoming the physical spin-up and readiness probe delays inherent in microservices container orchestration. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
117 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 75 0 R
/T (Predictive Time-Series Pipeline: Developing multi-step forecasting models comparing statistical baselines \(ARIMA\), machine learning ensembles \(Random Forest, XGBoost\), and deep sequence models \(LSTM, GRU\) to forecast CPU utilization, memory demand, and request arrival rates. Closed-Loop Kubernetes Control: Building a custom auto-scaling control loop that interacts directly with the Minikube/Kubernetes cluster REST API to execute pre-emptive pod scaling actions. Quantifiable Outcomes: Minimizing prediction error \(MAE and RMSE\), eliminating transient SLA violations under synthetic burst traffic, and achieving a 20% to 30% reduction in cluster compute over-provisioning and energy usage. )
/E (Predictive Time-Series Pipeline: Developing multi-step forecasting models comparing statistical baselines \(ARIMA\), machine learning ensembles \(Random Forest, XGBoost\), and deep sequence models \(LSTM, GRU\) to forecast CPU utilization, memory demand, and request arrival rates. Closed-Loop Kubernetes Control: Building a custom auto-scaling control loop that interacts directly with the Minikube/Kubernetes cluster REST API to execute pre-emptive pod scaling actions. Quantifiable Outcomes: Minimizing prediction error \(MAE and RMSE\), eliminating transient SLA violations under synthetic burst traffic, and achieving a 20% to 30% reduction in cluster compute over-provisioning and energy usage. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
