<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 76 0 R
/T (Regressive Integrated Moving Average \(ARIMA\) and Holt-Winters Exponential Smoothing. While effective for periodic, stationary load patterns, these models struggle with highly dynamic, non-linear cloud workloads. Tree-based ensemble learning models \(Random Forest, XGBoost\) improved non-linear feature handling by incorporating lag metrics. Recently, recurrent deep learning architectures \(LSTM and GRU\) demonstrated state-of-the-art capability in learning long-range temporal dependencies and non- stationary traffic spikes. )
/E (Regressive Integrated Moving Average \(ARIMA\) and Holt-Winters Exponential Smoothing. While effective for periodic, stationary load patterns, these models struggle with highly dynamic, non-linear cloud workloads. Tree-based ensemble learning models \(Random Forest, XGBoost\) improved non-linear feature handling by incorporating lag metrics. Recently, recurrent deep learning architectures \(LSTM and GRU\) demonstrated state-of-the-art capability in learning long-range temporal dependencies and non- stationary traffic spikes. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
