578 0 obj
<<
/Title (Moderncloud applications host highly dynamic web services that experience continuously changing and unpredictable user workloads. Traditional reactive auto-scaling models \(e.g., standard Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler\) trigger infrastructure adjustments only after physical metric thresholds \(such as CPU utilization exceeding 80%\) are breached. Because launching new container replicas or virtual machines incurs a non-negligible initialization lag \(ranging from 30 to 180 seconds\), reactive systems respond too late during high-velocity burst traffic. This provisioning delay results in transient resource exhaustion, latency spikes, and severe Service Level Agreement \(SLA\) violations.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 543 0 R
/Next 579 0 R
>>
endobj
579 0 obj
<<
/Title (This research project aims to design, implement, and validate an intelligent, closed-loop demand prediction and proactive auto-scaling framework for dynamic cloud infrastructure. By replacing standard reactive mechanisms with predictive time-series deep learning architectures \(including Gated Recurrent Units [GRU] and Long Short-Term Memory [LSTM] networks\), the system anticipates workload spikes 3 to 5 minutes into the future. The scaling engine programmatically communicates with the Kubernetes API to adjust container pod replicas pre-emptively, eliminating cold-start delays, preventing SLA penalties, and optimizing overall operational costs and cluster energy consumption.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 543 0 R
/Prev 578 0 R
>>
endobj
